1
00:00:55,390 --> 00:00:57,737
Thank you all for coming to my talk this evening.

2
00:00:57,737 --> 00:01:00,687
 It’s nice to see so many people in the audience.

3
00:01:00,687 --> 00:01:08,419
For those of you who don’t know very much about ‘Connection’, let me start by giving you some background information about it.


4
00:01:08,419 --> 00:01:15,400
‘Connection’ is a British organisation that facilitates homestays all over the globe. 

5
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:29,835
This organisation prides itself on matching tens of thousands of host families with guests every single year, allowing travellers to discover a country’s culture in a way like no other.

6
00:01:29,835 --> 00:01:51,772
Homestays are ideal for both travellers and homeowners, enabling inter-cultural exchanges and the development of life-long friendships, while providing travellers with often discounted accommodation costs, and host families with a steady income from the comfort of their own homes.

7
00:01:51,772 --> 00:02:07,523
The homestay experience is particularly popular with university exchange students looking for a more genuine insight into their country of choice, and an unrivalled opportunity to develop their language skills.

8
00:02:07,523 --> 00:02:17,841
The homestay experience is truly unique and once-in- a-lifetime, and one that you will likely remember for the rest of your lives.

9
00:02:17,841 --> 00:02:28,027
It is important to note, however, that some people will find it difficult to adapt to the new country, with many enduring what is known as ‘culture shock’.

10
00:02:28,027 --> 00:02:38,249
Connection’s advice for those suffering from culture shock, is to go out and make as many friends as possible, no matter how difficult you may find it.

11
00:02:38,249 --> 00:02:47,216
Friends are guaranteed to help you feel more integrated as part of the local society, and show you some great places to hang out.

12
00:02:47,216 --> 00:03:02,913
At first, it might seem extremely challenging to overcome the language barrier between you and your host family; however, you will find that you quickly overcome this and develop a very close and almost familial relationship.

13
00:03:02,913 --> 00:03:19,157
Many of our travellers have suggested that  they have found discussing their hobbies and other interests with their host families is the best way to overcome any barriers, since you are more than likely to find something you share in common.


14
00:03:19,157 --> 00:03:27,845
For example, you might find that you are both passionate about football, and end up playing in the local field every week. 

15
00:03:27,845 --> 00:03:44,031
One of our guests undertaking a homestay in a rural area of the UK told us that she and her host now take a Tai Chi class together upon a hilltop at sunrise, calling the experience ‘absolutely breathtaking’.


16
00:03:44,031 --> 00:04:07,558
After the first few weeks, you will find your understanding of the people around you and their culture deepens by leaps and bounds, and you will soon become one of the locals. Our hosts, in over 140 countries, turn a location into a culture, time into experience and strangers into friends.

17
00:04:42,674 --> 00:04:47,065
So how can you find out about applying for a homestay? 

18
00:04:47,065 --> 00:04:58,790
The best way would be to visit Connection’s website, www.connection.com, and contact one of their friendly advisors for more information.

19
00:04:58,790 --> 00:05:14,357
Once you have confirmed your interest in the service, we would strongly advise that you remain in close contact with the registration office, which will send you several emails keeping you up-to-date with potential matches in your country of choice.

20
00:05:14,357 --> 00:05:26,699
Once registered, Connection will require you to send various documents, and will act as an intermediary between you and the host family prior to final confirmation and payment.

21
00:05:26,699 --> 00:05:35,579
During this stage, Connection will ask you to Q16 provide two photos, one for the host family, and the other for our own records.

22
00:05:35,579 --> 00:05:39,555
Please ensure that you sign the back of each photo.

23
00:05:39,555 --> 00:05:55,392
Due to the nature of the service Connection provides, security is an absolute must, and they will ask you to send in photocopies of your passport, birth certificate, and a bank statement as confirmation of your identity.

24
00:05:55,392 --> 00:06:06,325
On receipt of these documents, the official process will begin and your bank account will be debited for the initial deposit of £200.

25
00:06:06,325 --> 00:06:18,262
If you haven’t received any acknowledgement confirming receipt of these documents from us within seven working days, please contact
the main office.


26
00:06:18,262 --> 00:06:35,823
As I mentioned before, due to the nature of the organisation, Connection operates a meticulous screening process, and applicants will undergo an interview in our head office in London, with exceptions made in extreme circumstances.

27
00:06:35,823 --> 00:06:43,981
After your interview, it may take us several weeks to carry out the decision process, so please be patient with us.

28
00:06:43,981 --> 00:06:53,281
If you would like a fast-track service, please indicate this on your application and we will notify you of the additional charges. 

29
00:06:53,281 --> 00:07:01,859
Finally, once we have come to a result about your application, you will receive a decision in the post. 

30
00:07:01,859 --> 00:07:08,429
If you do not receive an offer of placement, we will refund your deposit within 7 working days.